SpeechBrain ECAPA Speaker Verifier ONNX

This package contains a portable ONNX conversion of the SpeechBrain ECAPA-TDNN
speaker embedding model and a frozen SpeechBrain filterbank matrix for
preprocessing.

This package does not train or author the upstream speaker embedding model. It
repackages and converts the upstream SpeechBrain model to ONNX so it is easier
to run locally in applications that provide their own ONNX Runtime integration.

Model attribution:
- Upstream model: speechbrain/spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb
- Upstream project: https://github.com/speechbrain/speechbrain
- Upstream model page: https://huggingface.co/speechbrain/spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb
- Upstream license: Apache-2.0
- Upstream training data: VoxCeleb1 and VoxCeleb2 training data
- Upstream expected audio: 16 kHz single-channel recordings

Conversion notes:
- The ECAPA embedding network was exported from the upstream SpeechBrain
  PyTorch checkpoint to ONNX for local inference.
- The model was not retrained.
- The model weights remain derived from the upstream SpeechBrain release.
- The SpeechBrain filterbank matrix used by the reference path was frozen into
  model/fbank-80x201-f32.bin so applications can reproduce compatible
  preprocessing without Python, pip, PyTorch, torchaudio, or SpeechBrain at
  runtime.

References requested by the upstream model card:
- SpeechBrain: A General-Purpose Speech Toolkit, Ravanelli et al.,
  arXiv:2106.04624, 2021.
- ECAPA-TDNN: Emphasized Channel Attention, Propagation and Aggregation in
  TDNN Based Speaker Verification, Desplanques, Thienpondt, and Demuynck,
  Interspeech 2020, pages 3830-3834.

Limitations:
- The upstream SpeechBrain model card states that the SpeechBrain team does
  not provide a warranty for performance achieved on other datasets.
- This ONNX conversion is not a retrained model and does not add any upstream
  performance warranty.

This package is not affiliated with or endorsed by SpeechBrain.
